Third-party dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project depends on the following third-party libraries. Each remains under
its own license; none are modified or forked. GPL and AGPL licensed artifacts
are deliberately excluded (see CONTRIBUTING.md).

  com.github.wendykierp:JTransforms          BSD 2-Clause
  com.microsoft.onnxruntime:onnxruntime      MIT
  com.anthropic:anthropic-java               MIT
  info.picocli:picocli                       Apache-2.0
  com.fasterxml.jackson.*                    Apache-2.0
  org.slf4j:slf4j-api                        MIT
  ch.qos.logback:logback-classic             EPL-1.0 / LGPL-2.1
  com.tagtraum:jipes                         LGPL-2.1
  com.tagtraum:ffsampledsp-complete          LGPL-2.1 (bundles FFmpeg natives, LGPL-2.1+)
  org.audiveris:proxymusic                   LGPL-3.0

One dependency is vendored as source rather than resolved from Maven Central,
so the enforcer's banned-artifact list never sees it -- its licence position is
executed against the built artifact by tools/check-sherpa-native.sh instead:

  sherpa-onnx (eolivelli/sherpa-onnx, a fork of k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx
  carrying two patches under review as k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx#3873)  Apache-2.0
    a git submodule under third_party/; its Java API is compiled into builds
    that carry the sherpa profile and ships inside mw.jar, unmodified; its
    native library is built locally with TTS off, keeping the GPL-3.0 espeak
    fork out of the link, and is never redistributed

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Machine learning models
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No model weights are distributed with this software. Stages that need one
fetch it on first use into a local cache directory, checksummed, with its
provenance written beside it, and each remains under its own license. The list
records what has been chosen so far:

  onnxcrepe (pitch tracking)       MIT     github.com/yqzhishen/onnxcrepe
  basic-pitch (note transcription) Apache-2.0  github.com/spotify/basic-pitch
  Spleeter 2stems (separation)     MIT     doi:10.21105/joss.02154
    weights MIT per the Spleeter JOSS paper (the repository README licenses
    only the code); as ONNX, converted by sherpa-onnx (Apache-2.0)
  wav2vec2-base-960h (lyric alignment)  Apache-2.0  (Meta AI)
    as ONNX from the Xenova export of facebook/wav2vec2-base-960h
  Qwen3-ASR 0.6B (lyric transcription)  Apache-2.0  (Alibaba)
    code and weights alike; as the int8 ONNX export published by
    sherpa-onnx (Apache-2.0) in its own release archive

Models under non-commercial terms (CC BY-NC-SA), including the madmom
pretrained models and the Open-Unmix "umxl" weights, are deliberately NOT used.
Nor are models whose weights carry terms narrower than their code. Demucs is the
example: its code is MIT and its author states that the weights are provided for
scientific purposes only, whatever licence a third-party re-upload is tagged
with.

